# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Secrets / local config
.env

# Generated artifacts
chroma_db/
.cache/

# Runtime data written into data/ at request time. These were untracked but NOT
# ignored, so a plain `git add -A` after any real use would have committed whatever
# documents users uploaded and every question/answer pair they rated.
data/uploads/
data/feedback.jsonl
# Fetched corpus: real filings, large, and re-fetchable with scripts/fetch_corpus.py.
# data/SOURCES.md is deliberately NOT ignored — it is the provenance and licence record
# for a public repo and should travel with it.
data/corpus/
# Exported vector space for the Embedding Projector (F26): derived from the index,
# regenerate with scripts/export_embeddings.py. A few MB of floats, not source.
data/embeddings/
# Evaluation run history (scripts/run_log.py). Machine-local by design: it records what
# *this* machine measured, including runs from dirty trees, and every run appends a line.
# Committing it would conflict on every eval and mix results from different hardware and
# models into one series. The curated narrative that belongs to the repo is
# docs/RUN-LOG.md; this is the raw append-only log behind it.
data/runs.jsonl
# Ragas-generated questions (scripts/generate_testset.py). Regenerable, and deliberately
# not committed: it is unverified LLM output, and a file sitting in eval/ next to the
# hand-written qa_dataset.jsonl reads as an endorsed dataset. Generate it, read it, use
# it — do not let it accrete authority by being checked in.
eval/qa_generated.jsonl
